    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d188">

                <pb facs="0233" n="1067" xml:id="pg1067"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/10618a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Sharp</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-10-11T17:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 11, 1918, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5873. For McFadden [from
                    War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 366. Stetson. Japan may soon request Paris and London
                    for inclusion in inter-Allied enemy trading listing and licensing committees on
                    basis principle unification of enemy trading lists and stricter administrative
                    control. England will assent to inclusion Japan if Japan requests it. We deem it
                    of great importance that Japan should participate conferences Paris and London,
                    as well as Washington. French Blockade representative, Washington, is
                    telegraphing his Government accordingly.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
